# PRD: Consistent Core and MCP flow from artefact recording to closeout

Status: draft
Gate: PRD
Gate approval: open
Owner: Arndt Gold (product decisions); Codex (drafting)
Date: 2026-10-10
Run: core-mcp-flow-coherence-20261010-01
Language: en
Traceability contract: criteria-chain-v1

## 1. Product Scope

Deliver the approved UR as one integrated operational flow aligned with existing architecture R-04. A user or agent can inspect the bound state, obtain supported authoring/operation guidance, record actual work through the existing owners, prepare the exact gate presentation, record a new deliberate human response, apply a supported source revision and complete governance with consistent backlog/cockpit results. CLI and MCP describe the same Core meaning. The app reads and presents the relevant resulting state and evidence.

The first increment includes the existing structured_slice and structured_delivery modes plus regression compatibility for Quick Task. The candidate corpus is bounded to the two cockpit-run collections and the assessment; it is not a general API-discovery product. The supported capability set is:

| Capability | Included outcome | Existing boundary retained |
|---|---|---|
| Observe state and applicable contracts | Current bound state, typed next operation/actor, effect classification, supported inputs/forms and exact diagnostics | Read-only inspection never repairs, selects a foreign Run or grants authority |
| Record internal work and sources | Brownfield/route, UX, approved-TP preparation/CD+Tests and required review/evidence/artefact registration can be recorded without routine control-table edits | Recording reflects actual analysis/review/work; applicable gate and seal ordering remain enforced |
| Prepare presentation | Exact eligible gate material and presentation identity/digests are prepared and returned | This is preparatory writing, not a human decision |
| Record deliberate approval | Existing bound approval command records a new exact response with operation identity, receipt and current observation | Cooperative provenance explicitly retained; no inferred/independent human proof |
| Revise supported sources | Existing permitted early revision and late structured CD+Tests preview/apply/recovery capabilities remain describable and accessible | Unsupported lifecycle/gate cases remain unsupported; no automatic approved-source edits |
| Complete governance | Required OR, applicable obligations, lifecycle and backlog pointer are consistently recorded or recovered | QA/UAT where applicable still required; completion neither performs nor requires Git/publication |
| Present current decision evidence | Current identifiable QA/UAT evidence, replaced history, unknown applicability and truthful version links | No fabricated historic binding, alternative QA decision or app-side policy |

MCP offers suitable operation-specific access to this set rather than an unrestricted replacement for Run State Markdown. Exact tool count, commands, schema fields and writer convergence are SD decisions. Existing adapter fields remain compatible or follow an explicit transition plan. No MCP write is exposed before its Core eligibility, semantics and recovery are designed and qualified.

Delivery stages have dependencies: shared state/operation/completion meaning; usable owner contracts and consistent authoring/evidence interpretation; bound writer flow/recovery; MCP and targeted app integration; then qualification of the complete chain. A partial stage cannot satisfy whole-run acceptance while another consumer still contradicts the same state.

## 2. UX Intent And Success

- primary_user_intent: Know what is currently true, what remains open and who can perform the next step without reconciling contradictory sources or finding hidden invocation syntax.
- success_signal: For a bound observation, current state and next operation agree across surfaces; supported routine actions use described contracts; completion and remaining obligations are trustworthy.
- primary_decision_or_action: Inspect exact applicable material, perform an eligible operation, deliberately decide at the pending gate, request a permitted revision, recover a concrete failure or complete governance.
- input_analysis: UX_INTENT_DEFINITION.md is ready; it is subordinate to the approved UR and this PRD upon approval.
- benefit_boundary: Less search and manual bookkeeping are measured for defined scenarios. No claim that all code inspection disappears or every weaker model performs better.

## 3. Working Modes And Effective State

| Working mode | Effective state | Authority | Primary visible owner |
|---|---|---|---|
| Observe/status | Current bound source/Run revision, prerequisites, gate, actor and operation | Existing canonical Core evaluator | Invoking agent/CLI/MCP observation or cockpit current view |
| Prepare/record | Draft/registered/checked/approved distinctions; confirmed operation effect separate from fresh current state | Existing relevant Core writer plus evaluator | Invoking result and corresponding current views |
| Await human decision | Exact eligible presentation prepared; approval still pending | Existing presentation/approval owner | Bound gate presentation in the existing agent interaction |
| Revise source | Preview causes no source change; allowed apply renews sources and dependent obligations | Existing source-revision authority | Impact preview/result and current state/history |
| Recover | Uncertain response, known receipt or pending transaction are explicit; only applicable recovery is eligible | Existing operation/receipt/recovery owner | Invoking error/result with responsible actor and bounded next action |
| Closeout | Applicable QA/UAT/OR and other obligations determine eligibility; incomplete synchronization is explicit | Existing closeout/evaluation/backlog responsibility | Agent/CLI/MCP effect/current result; cockpit shows current meaning |
| Completed/history | Governance completed; historic material remains available; no current repeat OR obligation | Existing canonical completion/evidence evaluation | Current status and deliberately separate history |

Visible state types are current observation, confirmed historical effect, registered draft, checked draft, documented approval, internal work, human decision pending, missing prerequisite, validation error, unsupported operation, transient unavailability, recovery required, unknown evidence association, superseded history and completed governance. Technical owners/components implementing these roles are determined by SD.

## 4. Activation, Blockers, Recovery And Transitions

Existing Request Activation binds an explicit delivery intent to its target/Run. Pure status remains read-only. Opening a document or changing a view does not approve or invoke a write. Each operation revalidates its exact expected state and applicable gate/source/presentation binding. The actor can obtain concrete supported-input guidance before invoking it.

Missing prerequisites name the responsible actor and applicable next step. Stale/foreign bindings, invalid seal or incompatible runtime block the dependent operation. Malformed inputs name source/field/form and supported correction. Unsupported revision/lifecycle states do not turn into raw edits. Busy/read/check unavailability remains unavailable; a supported repeat action is visible. A lost write acknowledgement shows effect uncertainty and retains original operation identity where replay is supported. Conflict/concurrent change/pending transaction requires the existing bounded recovery, not blind repetition or a new invented decision.

Transitions preserve distinct meanings: draft -> registered -> exact presented material -> new deliberate response -> confirmed decision effect -> current evaluated next operation; analysis/review registration -> satisfied internal input, not human approval; revision preview -> allowed apply -> changed dependencies and renewed obligations; failed/uncertain response -> inspect/retry/recover -> fresh current state; QA pass before approval -> human decision pending; revise/block -> owned obligation; accepted applicable QA/UAT plus valid OR/requirements -> governance completion. Completed -> history inspection does not reopen closeout.

View or interaction closure ends that interaction without approval/completion. Actual backend teardown is evidenced separately. Old asynchronous read/check results must not revive superseded state after refresh, revision or expiry. The app remains a reader of Core descriptions and retains existing draft-check interactions; this increment introduces no app gate-approval or general writer buttons.

## 5. Acceptance Criteria

- criterion_id: AC-001; working_mode: observe and record; source_state: same bound source/Run revision, including a source-revised run with completed UX; trigger/action: evaluate state before and after each supported recording or approval; expected effective state: complete prerequisite/gate/completion meaning and current next operation agree across Core, writer follow-up, Inspect, dispatcher, CLI/MCP, backlog and cockpit; visible feedback: same current state/actor/action and explicit observed revision; blocker/failure behavior: stale, ambiguous or unavailable current state is rejected or identified; recovery/next action: refresh/rebind through the current owner; observable success: revised-source and no-source-revision chains contain no false UX/PRD fallback or contradictory next step; required evidence: shared-state contract and whole-chain comparisons including real disposable-target writes.
- criterion_id: AC-002; working_mode: permitted continuation; source_state: eligible structured step with fulfilled prerequisites; trigger/action: vary semantically equivalent display wording then request continuation; expected effective state: stable typed operation controls routing; visible feedback: useful descriptive next step without executable prose dependency; blocker/failure behavior: unmet prerequisite or stale binding still blocks; recovery/next action: satisfy the named condition then reevaluate; observable success: wording changes do not alter routing or permission and adapters introduce no separate policy map; required evidence: policy/dispatcher and transport regression scenarios.
- criterion_id: AC-003; working_mode: authoring and contract inspection; source_state: eligible unapproved UR/PRD/SD/TP or eligible operation input; trigger/action: obtain current supported forms and validate defined valid/invalid examples; expected effective state: metadata, readiness and presentation agree with executing owners and version; visible feedback: source/field/form, expected condition, actual defect where available and permitted correction; blocker/failure behavior: malformed, unsupported and technically unavailable are distinct, never success; recovery/next action: correct permitted input or route unsupported capability; observable success: valid examples pass both checks and presentation while invalid examples require no parser-source search to understand correction; required evidence: authoring-format corpus, metadata/check/presentation comparisons and invalid-input diagnostics.
- criterion_id: AC-004; working_mode: internal recording and preparation; source_state: earliest eligible internal step or artefact/review registration; trigger/action: record actual Brownfield/route, UX, preparation, CD+Tests, reviews and sources/evidence in the prescribed order; expected effective state: required pointer, relationship, seal and relevant result are recorded coherently through existing owners; visible feedback: confirmed effect/new revision and next permitted operation; blocker/failure behavior: missing inputs, wrong gate/order or fabricated completion do not satisfy prerequisites; recovery/next action: correct named input/order or follow pending-transaction recovery; observable success: the supported routine lifecycle requires zero hand-edits to control tables and does not turn review evidence into QA approval; required evidence: actual disposable-target recording chain, relationship/seal checks and invalid-order cases.
- criterion_id: AC-005; working_mode: prepare and decide; source_state: eligible exact gate artefact awaiting approval; trigger/action: prepare presentation, show it and record a new exact deliberate response through the existing typed authority; expected effective state: preparation remains distinct from approval; approved material, receipt and fresh current observation retain exact binding; visible feedback: presentation identity/artefact reference, pending decision, then confirmed effect and current next step with cooperative assurance; blocker/failure behavior: old, foreign, stale or absent presentation/reply cannot approve; recovery/next action: prepare current material and obtain a new deliberate response where required; observable success: valid human-response path succeeds and negative cases preserve gate/approval integrity; required evidence: presentation/approval positive and negative flows and actual MCP command results.
- criterion_id: AC-006; working_mode: supported source revision; source_state: existing revision-capable lifecycle state; trigger/action: obtain capability, preview impact and invoke supported bound application/recovery; expected effective state: preview writes no revised source and apply enforces invalidation/current renewed obligations while preserving exact historical sources; visible feedback: supported versus unsupported state, impact and result/history are explicit; blocker/failure behavior: unsupported lifecycle, stale proposal/source or conflicting operation is rejected without raw-edit fallback; recovery/next action: existing revision inspection/recovery or current earliest owner; observable success: retained and invalidated approvals match supported dependency policy; required evidence: existing early path and late CD+Tests preview/apply/negative/recovery qualification, no broadened revision policy.
- criterion_id: AC-007; working_mode: retry/recovery; source_state: exposed write with lost response, same identity or pending/conflicting/concurrent state; trigger/action: inspect receipt/current state and perform only supported same-operation retry or recovery; expected effective state: known effect, uncertainty, current observation and recovery are distinguishable without duplicate decisions/effects; visible feedback: receipt/revision or exact conflict/recovery reason plus actor and next action; blocker/failure behavior: changed payload, stale concurrent state or unresolved transaction cannot be silently accepted; recovery/next action: documented operation-specific inspect/replay/recovery preserving original identity where supported; observable success: every exposed writer has tested behavior and no unsupported idempotence guarantee; required evidence: lost-acknowledgement, payload conflict, concurrent change and persistence-boundary cases for each exposed write family.
- criterion_id: AC-008; working_mode: operation-result observation; source_state: historical confirmed receipt exists while Run/source changed or current observation fails; trigger/action: repeat/inspect the operation result; expected effective state: receipt describes its original effect, fresh observation describes current revision or unavailability; visible feedback: confirmed past effect and current applicability/unknown current state separately; blocker/failure behavior: historical next step is not presented as currently permitted; recovery/next action: refresh current state when available without reapproving old content; observable success: replay after later revision never reverts or misrepresents current control; required evidence: historical-receipt/current-observation and unavailable-reader scenarios.
- criterion_id: AC-009; working_mode: governance closeout; source_state: existing Quick Task or structured mode with satisfied or missing applicable quality/approval/OR requirements; trigger/action: invoke bounded closeout and interrupt synchronization at defined persistence boundaries; expected effective state: OR, lifecycle and backlog pointer are complete together or visibly recoverable; visible feedback: fulfilled versus missing obligations, pending recovery or completed governance; blocker/failure behavior: missing/invalid requirement cannot yield clean completion; recovery/next action: complete actual missing requirement or recover synchronization without repeating fulfilled decisions; observable success: both structured modes and Quick Task have consistent completion, completed runs do not request OR again and no Git/publication action occurs; required evidence: positive/negative closeout and interrupted synchronization tests with actual durable records.
- criterion_id: AC-010; working_mode: decision evidence and history; source_state: current QA/UAT material plus superseded or unstructured historical references; trigger/action: prepare decision or view current undertaking; expected effective state: applicable current material is selected using available exact bindings, replaced material is history and unresolved applicability is unknown; visible feedback: current evidence, explicit history/unknown association and truthful available document-version links; blocker/failure behavior: file presence/history order alone cannot establish current prerequisite or pass; recovery/next action: inspect/record proper evidence through existing owner; observable success: UAT summary does not select obsolete first rows as current and no historical binding/approval is fabricated; required evidence: revised-source/current-history corpus and Core/presenter/cockpit comparisons.
- criterion_id: AC-011; working_mode: app observation and existing draft check; source_state: current/expired/superseded result with relevant refresh/view/session changes; trigger/action: open exact document, inspect sources/history, refresh, change view and perform retained draft-check retry; expected effective state: current Core interpretation and exact-version proof remain authoritative; stale result never revives; visible feedback: coherent next step, current evidence, truthful link state and explicit unavailable/expired check; blocker/failure behavior: missing exact version, expiry or changed snapshot produces the existing truthful unavailable/renewal state; recovery/next action: current read/check path and visible retry where supported; observable success: implemented document/draft findings retain binding and lifecycle behavior, native relevant focus/scroll interactions remain stable where tested; required evidence: Core/app regression plus actually observed affected host interactions, with unobserved native behavior disclosed.
- criterion_id: AC-012; working_mode: transport invocation and compatibility; source_state: same valid/invalid/stale operation exposed through Core/CLI/MCP and existing readable clients/receipts; trigger/action: execute matching positive, rejection and recovery scenarios; expected effective state: semantic parity with existing owner authority and explicit compatible transition; visible feedback: consistent outcome/reason/binding and capability/version/assurance; blocker/failure behavior: unsupported contract or integrity mismatch fails explicitly; recovery/next action: supported compatible path, with new write access disableable without deleting receipts; observable success: actual MCP writes match corresponding Core/CLI meaning, legacy readable data remain usable or follow qualified transition; required evidence: real transport tests, compatibility corpus and rollback plan; no adapter policy duplicates.
- criterion_id: AC-013; working_mode: runtime/host qualification; source_state: candidate build and required host/session evidence; trigger/action: test the specified actual candidate flow/resource and record observations; expected effective state: source/build/protocol/browser/native results are distinguished and bound to candidate identity; visible feedback: tested runtime/resource/host and missing evidence are explicit; blocker/failure behavior: unreachable or unobserved host does not become success or stronger response proof; recovery/next action: prepared owner-bound observation or precise external gap; observable success: claims match performed checks, teardown is not inferred from tab closure and cooperative assurance remains honest; required evidence: actual installed MCP exercise in the chosen host and native app evidence only for affected claims; TP selects exact bounded observations.
- criterion_id: AC-014; working_mode: integrated delivery and benefit evaluation; source_state: fixed baseline corpus matching approved lifecycle with same or explicitly separated model/runtime/host conditions; trigger/action: execute before/after scenarios and evaluate whole chain; expected effective state: all dependent stages satisfy the common design and protected constraints; visible feedback: measured required searches/manual edits, schema failures, wrong next steps, redundant prompts and successful recovery separate from legitimate decisions/external actions; blocker/failure behavior: a still-contradictory consumer or weakened checks prevents whole-run acceptance; recovery/next action: correct the owning stage and rerun affected chain; observable success: supported routine corpus has zero undocumented invocation/parser discovery steps or control-table hand-edits, no false next step and preserved negative protections; required evidence: retained baseline/after comparison and whole-run report; model-specific improvement only if actually measured.
- criterion_id: AC-015; working_mode: protected behavior and localized presentation; source_state: foreign/completed Runs, existing exact document/draft behavior and registered presentation languages; trigger/action: run regression and render changed states in every registered language; expected effective state: approvals, foreign source bytes and existing document/readiness meaning remain protected, and localized state/action meaning matches Core; visible feedback: complete current/blocked/recovery/history messages in tested languages; blocker/failure behavior: foreign modifications, broken source proof or missing locale state fail qualification; recovery/next action: restore scoped implementation behavior, not rewrite reference approvals; observable success: no unrelated lifecycle change, approval transfer, implicit app writer or localization regression; required evidence: protected-baseline hashes, negative tests and rendered locale matrix.

## 6. Non-Goals

No new authority/store/orchestrator, universal code-understanding tool, tool-per-candidate multiplication, automatic approval, altered gate sequence or revision-policy expansion. No stronger independent human proof or blanket host/model qualification. No general test/owner inventory, product synthetic test profile, installer/restart work, general cockpit redesign or new app approval buttons. No foreign-run changes, inferred decisions or automatic Git/release/publication. Normal architecture/code review remains necessary.

## 7. Users And Roles

The human directing delivery owns deliberate intent and gate decisions. The agent prepares permissible artefacts/work and forwards exact new responses; it cannot claim independent human proof. Existing Core owners determine eligibility, recording, evidence applicability and state. QA alone makes final quality judgement. Review skills provide their actual evidence dimensions. CLI/MCP transport existing contracts; the cockpit presents current results and protected document/check behavior. Operational/native-host actions remain separately attributable when necessary.

## 8. Constraints

Use existing architecture operation ownership and R-04/R-05 separation. Expected pre-state binding, durable effect and observed post-state remain distinct. Per-operation repeatability must be qualified; no generic arbitrary-Run writer. Keep source revisions, historical presentations/approvals/receipts and foreign Runs protected. Unsupported lifecycle states remain explicit. SD must resolve mandatory compatibility/recovery/formats/current-evidence questions before implementation planning. Two distinct loaded runtime digests observed during planning are not byte-equivalence evidence. One Run does not mean one unstructured change or one test.

## 9. Evidence Requirements

Maintain a fixed baseline corpus from EVIDENCE_BROWNFIELD.md and the two candidate collections. Real writes use disposable targets, never live reference approvals. Include renewed UX/source and non-revised flows, all specified recording/presentation/decision/revision boundaries, Quick Task and both structured modes, historical receipts/evidence, stale/foreign binding, lost acknowledgement, payload conflict, concurrency and interrupted backlog synchronization. Compare same-bound Core/CLI/MCP/app meanings; trace every criterion through SD/TP rather than creating a second acceptance register.

For supported routine corpus, separately count undocumented invocation/parser searches, hand-edits, rejected schema calls, false follow-ups, redundant continuation prompts and successful recovery. Preserve legitimate approval/external-action counts and negative checks. Keep model, runtime and host fixed where a before/after claim needs comparability; otherwise report differences, not a performance conclusion. Synthetic tests establish contract/recovery evidence, not measured model or native-host quality.

Qualification must state actual commit/build/package/resource identity, installed MCP path, protocol exercise and any required native interaction/teardown observation. Later candidate changes invalidate only dependent evidence with applicability explained. Every changed localized presentation has a rendered matrix for all registered languages. No QA pass, completion or release is implied by this draft.

## 10. Risks And Open Questions

The main risk is exposing inconsistent or incomplete Core behavior more widely through MCP. A second mapping/parser/policy is not an acceptable fix. SD must decide complete proposed/persisted state preparation, typed operations, exact capabilities/tool shape, compatible legacy writer convergence, operation-specific retry/locking/receipt recovery, multi-record closeout, authoring interpretation and current-evidence applicability. Unknown historical association must remain honest. Product scope and acceptance above are concrete; technical decisions are owned deferrals below.

Related active scopes remain independent. Reuse the current repository baseline and recheck shared-owner changes during TP preparation. No retrospective completion or approval is owed to another Run. Native constraints may require a human observation; prepare its exact candidate/actions before asking. Broad installer remediation and independent host enforcement remain excluded.

## Approval Decisions

| Decision | Timing | Status | Resolution | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| One coherent first outcome | before_prd | resolved | Include the supported lifecycle capability set and its whole-flow failure/recovery acceptance in one Run with dependent stages; exclude general inventory/test profiles and universal code APIs. | Arndt Gold / product owner |
| Scope and human authority | before_prd | resolved | Preserve existing gates and cooperative assurance; typed approval reuses existing authority; app displays state/evidence without new approval buttons. | Arndt Gold / product owner |
| Revision and completion meaning | before_prd | resolved | Expose only supported existing revision states; governance completion requires applicable obligations and never implies Git/publication. | Arndt Gold / product owner |
| Evidence truth and acceptance | before_prd | resolved | Current exact-bound evidence, superseded history and unknown association differ. Actual parity/recovery and zero routine undocumented discovery/hand-edits define acceptance; weaker-model benefit only if measured. | Arndt Gold / product owner |
| Shared state, typed contracts and compatibility | later_sd | open | SD must resolve existing entry/catalog reuse, schemas/tool grouping, legacy behavior and compatible read/receipt transitions before its approval. | sd-definition / solution designer |
| Recovery, structured closeout and evidence interpretation | later_sd | open | SD must resolve per-operation repeatability and multi-record recovery, authoring interpretation and current evidence derivation before its approval; no accepted debt. | sd-definition / solution designer |
| Exact scenario/host/model/locale evidence plan | later_tp | open | TP maps every criterion/SD decision to concrete tasks/scenarios and proportional actual host evidence; no all-host/model performance promise. | Task/Test Plan owner |

Resolved rows are the proposal derived from approved UR/answered context for this PRD decision, not a claim that the PRD has already been approved. Later rows are technical/evidence planning obligations, not deferred user needs or hidden scope choices.

## 11. Next Step

Validate authoring readiness, register this PRD as derived from the exact approved UR through the canonical reviewed artefact writer, prepare a fresh bound presentation and obtain a new deliberate `Approval: PRD`. Only then draft SD and resolve its mandatory design decisions. No implementation permission is granted here.

## AGDF Approval Summary (de; source=en)

- Ziel: Einen konsistenten Ablauf von Artefakt-/Nachweiserfassung über Darstellung, bewusste Freigabe und unterstützte Revision bis zum Governance-Abschluss liefern. Derselbe gebundene Stand bedeutet in Core, CLI, MCP, Backlog und Cockpit dasselbe. Weniger Suchaufwand wird für definierte Fälle gemessen; bessere Leistung schwächerer Modelle ist noch nicht nachgewiesen.
- Umfang: Gemeinsame Zustands-/Operationssemantik; nutzbare Autoren- und Eingabeverträge; vorhandene Writer für interne Arbeit, Artefakte, Reviews, Darstellung, Freigabe und erlaubte Revision; strukturierter Abschluss mit Recovery; aktuelle Evidenz und gezielte App-Anzeige; tatsächliche MCP-Parität. Ein Run mit abhängigen Etappen und gemeinsamer Gesamtprüfung. Keine zweite Policy, automatische Freigabe, pauschale Hostzusage, App-Freigabebuttons, Installer-/Testinventar oder Git/Veröffentlichung.
- Entscheidungen: Der erste Umfang ist der zusammenhängende unterstützte Lebenszyklus. Vorhandene Freigabeautorität und kooperative Herkunft bleiben erhalten; die App zeigt aktuelle Ergebnisse. Revision bleibt auf bestehende erlaubte Zustände begrenzt. Governance-Abschluss ist von Git getrennt. Aktuelle Nachweise, ersetzte Historie und unbekannte Zuordnung sind unterscheidbar. SD muss gemeinsame Eigentümer, konkrete Verträge, Kompatibilität, Autoren-/Evidenzinterpretation und Recovery vor Freigabe klären. TP plant genaue Szenarien und erforderliche Host-/Sprachnachweise; diese technischen Punkte verschieben keine Produktentscheidung.
- AC-001: Alle Konsumenten beschreiben denselben aktuellen Stand, auch nach Quellenrevision mit erledigter UX-Analyse; keine falsche Rückkehr zu PRD.
- AC-002: Gleichbedeutend anderer Anzeigetext ändert keine Fortsetzung; der Core bestimmt die maschinenlesbare Operation und ihre Voraussetzungen.
- AC-003: Unterstützte Formen und Eingaben stimmen mit Autorenprüfung und Präsentation überein. Fehler nennen Quelle/Feld/Form und Korrektur ohne Suche im Parser.
- AC-004: Tatsächliche Analysen, Arbeit, Reviews und Artefakte werden in richtiger Reihenfolge samt Beziehung/Seal erfasst. Routine-Handedits entfallen; Erfassung erzeugt keine erfundene QA/Freigabe.
- AC-005: Exakte Präsentation und neue bewusste Antwort führen über den vorhandenen Freigabebefehl zum belegten Effekt. Alte, fremde oder veraltete Antworten bleiben ungültig.
- AC-006: Unterstützte Revision zeigt erst die Auswirkung und wendet dann gebunden an. Abhängige Freigaben werden korrekt erneuert; unzulässige Lebenszyklusfälle bleiben abgewiesen.
- AC-007: Verlorene Antwort, Wiederholung, Nutzlastkonflikt, Konkurrenz und unterbrochene Speicherung haben je Schreibvorgang getestete Recovery ohne doppelten Effekt oder erfundene Idempotenz.
- AC-008: Historischer Beleg und frischer aktueller Stand bleiben getrennt, auch wenn der aktuelle Leser ausfällt. Ein alter Folgeschritt wird nicht erneut erlaubt.
- AC-009: Quick Task und beide strukturierten Modi schließen OR, Lebenszyklus und Backlog konsistent oder sichtbar wiederherstellbar ab. Fehlende Voraussetzungen verhindern sauberen Abschluss; erledigte Runs verlangen keinen OR erneut und führen kein Git aus.
- AC-010: Aktuelle QA-/UAT-Entscheidungsnachweise folgen verfügbaren exakten Bindungen. Ersetzte Historie und unbekannte Zuordnung sind sichtbar; Dokumentlinks behaupten keine ungesicherte Fassung.
- AC-011: Die App zeigt Core-Zustand, nächsten Schritt und Evidenz; bestehende Dokument-/Entwurfsprüfungen bleiben gebunden. Refresh, veraltete Ergebnisse, Ablauf und geprüfte native Interaktionen bleiben korrekt.
- AC-012: Echte MCP-Aufrufe entsprechen Core/CLI für Erfolg, Ablehnung und Recovery. Vorhandene lesbare Verträge/Belege bleiben kompatibel oder folgen einem qualifizierten Übergang; neue Schreibzugriffe sind rücknehmbar.
- AC-013: Quellen-, Build-, Protokoll-, Browser- und native Hostnachweise benennen die tatsächlich geprüfte Fassung. Nicht beobachtete Hosts und bloß geschlossene Tabs liefern keine erfundene Qualifikation oder Herkunftssicherung.
- AC-014: Die gemeinsame Kette besteht definierte Vorher-/Nachher-Fälle mit null Routine-Handedits, null undokumentierter Aufruf-/Parser-Suche und keinen falschen Folgeangaben. Notwendige Entscheidungen, externe Aktionen und Negativkontrollen bleiben erhalten; Modellnutzen wird nur gemessen behauptet.
- AC-015: Fremde Runs/Freigaben, exakte Dokument-/Prüfsemantik und alle registrierten Darstellungssprachen bleiben durch entsprechende Regression und gerenderte Nachweise geschützt.
- Risiken und Quellen: Die freigegebene UR ist Produktgrundlage; fertiger Brownfield Review und bereite UX-Analyse sind analytische Eingaben. Bestehende Core-/Writer-/Proof-Eigentümer und R-04 bleiben maßgeblich. Multi-Datei-Recovery, ältere Vertragswege und freie historische Evidenz benötigen ausdrückliche SD-Entscheidungen; keine unbelegte Atomizität, stärkere menschliche Herkunft oder zweite Parserwahrheit. Tatsächliche Schreib-/Transport-/Hostprüfungen folgen erst dem freigegebenen Plan.
- Nächster Schritt: Diese neue PRD-Fassung mit `Approval: PRD` freigeben, Änderung verlangen oder ablehnen. Danach folgt SD; Implementierung bleibt bis TP und erforderlicher Vorbereitung gesperrt.
